# Everything the app writes about this machine.
#
# LUKE AI STUDIO runs from a git checkout on the user's own disk, so any file
# the app rewrites while it is used has to sit outside git. Tracking one is not
# a tidiness problem: the app changes it, and the next update that touches it is
# refused with
#
#   error: Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by
#   merge
#
# while `git checkout -- <file>` cannot clear it, because
# scripts/setup/git-local-state.sh marks these paths skip-worktree and git will
# not match a skip-worktree pathspec. The app creates every one of these on
# first use, and all 119 validation suites pass with the folder empty, so
# nothing is lost by keeping the whole directory out of git.
#
# This is anchored at the repository root: the copies under releases/ are
# frozen snapshots of past builds and stay tracked.
app/runtime-state/

# macOS metadata and local workspace junk
.fseventsd/
.Spotlight-V100/
.TemporaryItems/
.Trashes/
._*
*.orig
*.rej
*.backup
*.tmp-*
thai-tts.patch*
SuperTrader/




